; Picture table: id and address of each picture
;
; Records of 3 bytes: picture id (the location number), address of the picture
; data (word); terminated by $FF. Looked up with $9DBD (IX=$CC00) by $7F78,
; which sets $7F77 to the id found or $FF.
; .
; The picture is drawn at $7FA7 from a stream of commands (see Picture01):
; header (border, attribute), then $08 x y = move, $80-$FF = line, $40-$7F =
; fill, $20-$27 = attribute paint, $00 = end. The picture area is the top 128
; pixel rows (16 cell rows); y counts up from the bottom, row = $7F - y.
; .
; Picture ids are location numbers: $965B (called from $9630 with A = location)
; draws the picture of the location, if $B707 is non-zero ($6C7C: zero when N
; is held at start-up) and the picture is not suppressed by $95ED (carry set:
; the player cannot see, the screen is left black).
@label=PictureTable
b$CC00 DEFB $01
 $CC01 DEFW $CC43
 $CC03 DEFB $31
 $CC04 DEFW $CE77
 $CC06 DEFB $06
 $CC07 DEFW $CFB2
 $CC09 DEFB $0B
 $CC0A DEFW $D24E
 $CC0C DEFB $25
 $CC0D DEFW $D367
 $CC0F DEFB $2B
 $CC10 DEFW $D5B5
 $CC12 DEFB $26
 $CC13 DEFW $D713
 $CC15 DEFB $07
 $CC16 DEFW $D92A
 $CC18 DEFB $18
 $CC19 DEFW $DBA8
 $CC1B DEFB $23
 $CC1C DEFW $DD79
 $CC1E DEFB $0D
 $CC1F DEFW $E02C
 $CC21 DEFB $1F
 $CC22 DEFW $E049
 $CC24 DEFB $05
 $CC25 DEFW $E142
 $CC27 DEFB $1C
 $CC28 DEFW $E19F
 $CC2A DEFB $04
 $CC2B DEFW $E3FE
 $CC2D DEFB $20
 $CC2E DEFW $E47A
 $CC30 DEFB $10
 $CC31 DEFW $E6E4
 $CC33 DEFB $19
 $CC34 DEFW $E9EE
 $CC36 DEFB $08
 $CC37 DEFW $EC3E
 $CC39 DEFB $29
 $CC3A DEFW $EE43
 $CC3C DEFB $1A
 $CC3D DEFW $F001
 $CC3F DEFB $27
 $CC40 DEFW $F1E6
 $CC42 DEFB $FF
